# Implementation Roadmap

## Phase 1 — Renderer Feature Controls

**Goal:** Establish one clean master-control API before adding more renderer systems.

Horse:
- Add a shared renderer feature settings object with non-destructive master overrides for Lighting, Shadows, Environment, Global Illumination, Volumetrics and Gaussian Splat.
- Add a shared `Renderer::Quality` enum for systems that map a player-facing quality setting to internal tuning.
- Lighting off returns no effective lights without modifying ECS lights.
- Shadows off keeps lights but suppresses all effective shadow casting.
- Environment off suppresses environment/ambient contribution without modifying the `EnvironmentComponent`.
- GI off skips all GI build/update work.
- Volumetrics off skips the volumetric pass.
- Gaussian Splat off skips that pass.
- Add a non-destructive Camera master Active override.

GAME:
- Replace low-level GI/Volumetric controls with meaningful controls.
- Keep optional expensive systems disabled through master overrides by default, while their underlying scene configuration remains intact and ready to restore.

- [ ] Add renderer feature override API and tests.
- [ ] Add Camera master override and tests.
- [ ] Gate all current systems through the master overrides.
- [ ] Add quality preset API for Shadows, GI and Volumetrics.
- [ ] Simplify Renderer Debug menu.
- [ ] Simplify Camera Debug menu.

## Phase 2 — GPU Profiling

**Goal:** Measure actual GPU cost before optimizing or adding expensive passes.

Target information:

```text
Frame
├── Depth
├── Shadows
├── Visibility
├── PBR / Opaque
├── Transparent
├── GI
├── Volumetrics
├── Gaussian Splat
└── Present
```

- Use backend GPU timestamps only if SDL_GPU exposes a reliable path on the active backend.
- Do not label CPU command-recording time as GPU time.
- If portable timestamps are unavailable, keep the current CPU profiler and add backend-specific timing only when it can be implemented cleanly.

- [ ] Verify SDL_GPU timestamp/query support for current supported backends.
- [ ] Add renderer pass timing abstraction if reliable.
- [ ] Show high-level pass cost in the existing Performance window.

## Phase 3 — Depth Prepass + Hi-Z

**Goal:** Build the visibility foundation without changing image quality.

```text
Depth Prepass
    ↓
full-resolution depth
    ↓
Hi-Z mip pyramid
    ↓
conservative object-bound visibility tests
```

- Reuse Rasterizer depth.
- Build hierarchical depth with compute.
- Conservative occlusion only; false visible is acceptable, false hidden is not.
- Keep Frustum Culling independently switchable.

- [ ] Add Depth Prepass ownership.
- [ ] Build Hi-Z pyramid.
- [ ] Add Hi-Z debug visualization/status.

## Phase 4 — GPU Visibility + GPU-Driven Submission

**Goal:** Stop spending CPU/draw work on objects that cannot contribute to the frame.

- Use object/instance bounds, not triangle BVH nodes.
- Frustum test + Hi-Z occlusion test.
- Generate visible draw/instance list on GPU where SDL_GPU permits a clean implementation.
- Preserve CPU fallback where backend capability requires it.

- [ ] Add object bounds buffer.
- [ ] Add GPU visibility compute pass.
- [ ] Add compact visible instance list.
- [ ] Connect visible results to Rasterizer submission.

## Phase 5 — Forward+ / Clustered Lighting

**Goal:** Keep PBR cost scalable as scenes gain many lights.

```text
camera frustum
    ↓
screen tiles / depth clusters
    ↓
light assignment compute
    ↓
per-cluster light lists
    ↓
PBR shades only relevant lights
```

- Keep `LightComponent` API unchanged.
- Do not make game code understand clusters.
- Directional lights remain globally available where appropriate.
- Point/spot lights are culled into screen/depth clusters.

- [ ] Add cluster grid and buffers.
- [ ] Add light-cluster assignment.
- [ ] Change PBR light loop to cluster-local lights.
- [ ] Stress-test many point/spot lights.

## Phase 6 — Shadow System Upgrade

**Goal:** Improve both shadow quality and shadow cost.

```text
Shadows
├── Directional
│   ├── stable cascades
│   ├── texel snapping
│   ├── cascade blending
│   └── filtered sampling
├── Spot
│   └── atlas allocation
├── Point
│   └── array/cubemap allocation
└── Cache
    └── redraw only when light/casters change
```

Player controls remain only Enabled, Quality, Distance and visible Softness where supported.

- [ ] Stabilize cascades with texel snapping.
- [ ] Add cascade blending.
- [ ] Add PCF/filtered shadow sampling.
- [ ] Add shadow atlas/caching for local lights.

## Phase 7 — Ambient Occlusion

**Goal:** Add contact grounding and local depth without ray tracing.

Preferred direction: GTAO-style screen-space ambient occlusion using depth + normal information.

Player controls:
- Enabled
- Quality
- Strength
- Radius

